# AI VAPT Framework — environment variable template
# Copy to .env and fill in values as needed. .env is git-ignored.

# --- Default: local Ollama (no key required) ---
# The platform defaults to local Ollama with the official baseline model
# llama3.2:3b. Nothing below is required unless you opt into a hosted provider.

# --- Optional: OpenRouter provider (hosted API) ---
# NOT REQUIRED FOR GUI USE: both the web UI and Streamlit accept an API key at
# runtime from the "OpenRouter Setup" panel (Validate Connection). That key is
# held in browser/session memory only — it is never written here, never put
# into os.environ, and never stored in a run record or report. A page reload
# asks for it again.
# This variable is the optional SERVER-WIDE FALLBACK for shared, headless or
# CLI deployments where no browser session supplies a key.
# Opt-in only: explicitly select provider="openrouter" in the UI/API/request.
# If neither a runtime key nor this variable is available and OpenRouter is
# selected, create_assessor raises a clear configuration error AT CONSTRUCTION
# TIME. It NEVER silently switches to another provider.
# NOTE: this is deliberately different from OPENAI_API_KEY, whose missing-key
# behaviour is unchanged legacy behaviour (silent, explicitly-tagged
# deterministic fallback) so pre-existing OpenAI semantics are preserved.
# OpenRouter runs are recorded separately from the historical Ollama baseline
# experiments.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Hosted model slug to use when no explicit model is passed (optional).
# Any well-formed "vendor/model" slug is accepted (no allowlist). A value
# containing whitespace or control characters, or longer than 200 characters,
# raises ValueError when a client is constructed. Invalid -> falls back to the
# compiled-in default only where a non-raising path is required (health).
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct
# Request timeout in SECONDS (surfaced as a visible `timeout` error category).
# Clamped to 1..600s; values outside the range use the default below.
# OPENROUTER_TIMEOUT_S=60
# Retries before a rate-limit/timeouts surface as a terminal failure.
# Clamped to 0..5; values outside the range use the default below.
# OPENROUTER_MAX_RETRIES=2
# Attribution labels sent to the OpenRouter dashboard (optional).
# OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE=AI VAPT Framework
# OPENROUTER_APP_URL=

# --- Optional: OpenAI provider (for LLM assessment) ---
# If unset, the system uses local Ollama (llama3.2:3b) or deterministic fallback.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: GitHub token (for PoC corpus online fetch) ---
# If unset, the system uses the bundled offline PoC corpus.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
